/* @catalog — generated by `npm run catalog:generate`; do not edit by hand.
 * Internal
 *   Functions: make, create, mutation, errorCode, deferred, stored, newerProject
 *   Constants: actor, other, ordinary, provider, a1, a2
 *   Variables: harness
 * Tests
 *   - create retries are durable across flag rollback, mismatched intent rejected, and admin inventory is shared
 *   - manual draft revision races have one winner and replay survives later edits
 *   - inventory uses stable pagination and full counts; no reads enqueue work or expose actor identifiers
 *   - analysis admission is durable/idempotent and one active job per actor across concurrent requests
 *   - cancelled in-flight analysis retains actor and global capacity until its provider outcome is checkpointed
 *   - server checkpoint survives independent worker ticks and never overwrites manual edits
 *   - daily deployment budget serializes competing workers and never dispatches the losing reservation
 *   - uncertain provider outcomes consume the daily reservation and a new UTC day receives its own budget
 *   - nonliteral import flags cannot bypass capability admission
 *   - adoption applies selected fields atomically against baseline and replays exact receipt
 *   - manual selected-field conflict rejects adoption without partial changes
 *   - expired in-flight lease is uncertain and does not make another paid call
 *   - late previous lease result cannot replace recovered unknown outcome
 *   - role revocation before dispatch or completion stops new work and retains evidence
 *   - explicit cancellation retains in-flight outcome but prevents next chunk and generation replacement
 *   - unknown provider failures are bounded with no paid auto-retry; budget and grant boundaries persist
 *   - duplicate candidates include hidden ready identities without raw storage and prevent cross-album track reuse
 *   - analysis checkpoints retain admitted tag context despite later upload metadata changes
 *   - a draftless create stores public visibility while its receipt keeps the pre-public fingerprint
 *   - create-page and conversion-bridge retries admitted before the public default replay their hidden project, and conflicting retries fail
 *   - a project saved in a newer draft format is read-only: edits, analysis, adoption, decisions, publication and cover selection are refused unchanged
 *   - reads of a newer-format project expose only the v1 allowlist in detail, inventory and duplicate candidates
 *   - newer-format analyses, queued or with a chunk left in flight, hold no analysis capacity and are never claimed
 *   - an analysis claimed just before a newer release saved its project is released without a provider call or checkpoint
 * @end-catalog */

